* 14 Aug 26 Windows port - replaces groupadd, groupdel, usermod -aG, deluser
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    rc = !os_group(action, group, member)
*
*    action  ADD     create the group           member ignored
*            DEL     delete the group           member ignored
*            ADDMEM  add member to the group
*            DELMEM  remove member from the group
*
*    returns 0 success
*            1 the operation failed
*            2 a name is not valid, or the action is not one of the above
*            5 access denied: SD is not running elevated
*
*    WHY ONE SUBROUTINE RATHER THAN FOUR OS.EXECUTE LINES.  These four
*    operations appear at five call sites across CREATEA, DELACC and MODIFYA,
*    and every one of them needs the same elevation check and the same
*    quoting.  Section 5.14 asks for administrative capability to go in a
*    subroutine with something over it rather than in the caller, so that a
*    form can call the same code later instead of reimplementing it.
*
*    ADD and ADDMEM are idempotent: a group that already exists, or a member
*    already in it, is success rather than failure.  Account creation is
*    re-runnable that way, which matters because it can fail half finished -
*    the SD account and the Windows account are not created in one
*    transaction and nothing can make them so.
*
*    The Linux original passed "groupadd -U root,sdsys,<user>" to seed the
*    group's membership.  root and sdsys are Linux accounts with no Windows
*    counterpart, so only the SD user is added, by a separate ADDMEM call.
*
*    ELEVATION.  Local group changes need an elevated token; an ordinary SD
*    session has a UAC-filtered one and gets "System error 5, access is
*    denied".  Measured 14 Aug 2026.  The check is made explicitly rather
*    than read out of a failure message, because those are localised.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function os_group(action, group, member)
$catalog !os_group

deffun valid_os_name(name) calling '!valid_os_name'

   rc = 2
   set.status 0

   if not(valid_os_name(group)) then return rc

   act = upcase(action)

   if act = 'ADDMEM' or act = 'DELMEM' then
      if not(valid_os_name(member)) then return rc
   end

*  14 Aug 26 Windows port - SH1 names PowerShell, so the command IS the
*  script and there is no bash layer to quote against.  Both names have been
*  through !valid_os_name - letters, digits, dot, underscore and hyphen only -
*  so neither can carry a quote out of the strings below.

   ps = 'if (-not (New-Object Security.Principal.WindowsPrincipal('
   ps := '[Security.Principal.WindowsIdentity]::GetCurrent())).IsInRole('
   ps := '[Security.Principal.WindowsBuiltInRole]::Administrator)) { exit 5 }; '

   begin case
      case act = 'ADD'
         ps := 'if (Get-LocalGroup -Name "' : group : '" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) { exit 0 }; '
         ps := 'try { New-LocalGroup -Name "' : group : '" -Description "SD account group" -ErrorAction Stop | Out-Null } catch { exit 1 }; exit 0'

      case act = 'DEL'
         ps := 'try { Remove-LocalGroup -Name "' : group : '" -ErrorAction Stop } catch { exit 1 }; exit 0'

      case act = 'ADDMEM'
         ps := 'try { Add-LocalGroupMember -Group "' : group : '" -Member "' : member : '" -ErrorAction Stop } '
         ps := 'catch [Microsoft.PowerShell.Commands.MemberExistsException] { exit 0 } catch { exit 1 }; exit 0'

      case act = 'DELMEM'
         ps := 'try { Remove-LocalGroupMember -Group "' : group : '" -Member "' : member : '" -ErrorAction Stop } catch { exit 1 }; exit 0'

      case 1
         return rc
   end case

   os.execute ps

   rc = os.error()
   if rc # 0 then set.status rc

return rc
end

